# Rect corners and sharp versus rounded polygons, on paper, 192x128, each shape with a 2px dark ink outline.
# Top row, left to right: a red 48x36 rect with square corners; a blue 48x36 rect with r:12 so all four corners are
# visibly rounded; a green 48x36 rect with r:12,12,0,0 so only the two top corners are rounded and the two bottom
# corners are square.
# Bottom row, left to right: a gold triangle (poly 3) pointing up with sharp corners; a red pentagon with sharp
# corners and one vertex at the top; a blue 8-point star with a deep notch (inner radius 0.3 of the outer) so the
# points are thin spikes.
@artboard 192x128
@target shapes/corners.png

rect 48x36 at:32,32 fill:p.red stroke:p.ink,2
rect 48x36 r:12 at:96,32 fill:p.blue stroke:p.ink,2
rect 48x36 r:12,12,0,0 at:160,32 fill:p.green stroke:p.ink,2
poly 3 r:24 at:32,96 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,2
poly 5 r:24 at:96,96 fill:p.red stroke:p.ink,2
star 8 r:26 inner:.3 at:160,96 fill:p.blue stroke:p.ink,2
